    "current_complete_changed_entries": [
      {
        "id": "Q054",
        "question": "For Reincarnator, state the eligible player role, whether use is optional or mandatory, and its phase(s); then explain what results trigger Reincarnation, where is the replacement drawn from and which candidates are rejected, what happens on later losses, what old power remains, and under the original printed copying conditional, which powers may another alien copy and what happens when that copier loses?"
      },
      {
        "id": "Q120",
        "question": "With Human Super, may Human add eight and then discard the flare to zap itself? May it instead discard solely to zap without taking the plus eight? Does the +8 replace the normal +4 or stack with it? After taking +8, must Human discard the flare to self-Zap, or may it decline that extra step?"
      },
      {
        "id": "Q123",
        "question": "For Mind Wild, Reserve Wild and Vulch Super, must the flare be replayed for each later qualifying event in that encounter, or does one play last through the encounter? When is Vulch Super first played, and may Vulch collect that same Super through its effect? While Reserve Wild remains active, whose discarded cards of what type may its user take, and where do those cards go? Is each eligible Reserve Wild pickup compulsory or separately optional; if the user declines one, may it still take a later eligible discard? If several otherwise-eligible flares are discarded at the same time while Vulch Super is active, may its power apply to all of them or only one from that group?"
      },
      {
        "id": "Q148",
        "question": "Under the retained official Mind Wild erratum, when can the flare be played, which later draws does that one play intercept, what does the user do with each intercepted card, and may the information be shared? For each later qualifying deck draw, is interception compulsory or may the user decide separately?"
      },
      {
        "id": "Q167",
        "question": "Without a power changing ordinary compensation, how are its cards selected from the opponent's hand, may the recipient see their faces while selecting, and is seeing only their backs allowed?"
      },
      {
        "id": "Q168",
        "question": "After drawing the player-color destiny card that selects the first player, what happens to that card before play begins, and in which direction do ordinary turns pass?"
      }
    ],
